! A fixture, not a dictionary. A record whose tail waits for the unit after it,
! which is `[AFTER]`: the keys come first and the text the tail attaches to comes
! later.
!
! Nothing here reads that text. The tail only follows it, so the join is the
! host's: `[ORTHO_L]` is the same orthography a folded suffix key gets. The cases
! are chosen to agree with a plain join, because whether this machine has the
! orthography artifacts is a property of the machine and not of the mechanism.

! A tail and nothing else, so the stroke writes nothing at all.
KWRS	[AFTER]s[ORTHO_L][END]
! A body and a tail: "and" now, "too" after the next unit's word.
KWRT	and[AFTER]too[END]
